      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much money do I need to retire in India?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on your expenses, age and inflation. As a rough guide, a family spending ₹50,000 a month today and retiring in 30 years needs about ₹7.7 crore, assuming 6% inflation and 7% returns after retirement."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the 25x rule for retirement?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It says you need about 25 times your first year's expenses at retirement. The right multiple depends on how long retirement lasts and how much your money earns above inflation: the example on this page (25 years, 7% return, 6% inflation) needs about 22 times. Retiring earlier or earning less after retirement pushes it above 25 times."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What return should I assume?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For long-term planning, around 10–12% for an equity-heavy portfolio before retirement and 6–8% for a safer mix after retirement are common assumptions. Returns are not guaranteed."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is EPF enough for retirement?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For most people, no. EPF is a strong base, but salary growth and inflation usually mean you also need NPS, PPF or mutual fund investments."
      }
    }
  ]
